model-file MODEL [--limit N] [--max-bytes N] [--format json|text] describe`. Values the library refuses (ranges, conflicts between flags, unknown columns) come back as a tool error with the rule, the exit code and the repair.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"model-file\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"predict, eval, describe, importance, dump: the model file to read\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0,\"maximum\":1000000,\"default\":1000,\"description\":\"predict: the most rows in one page of predictions, at least 1. describe: the most category strings listed for each categorical column and the most rows of the importance table, at least 1 (a longer table lists the best ranks). runs list: the most run records listed, at least 1\"},\"max-bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0,\"maximum\":268435456,\"default\":16777216,\"description\":\"fit: the largest model file written, the limit predict and eval apply when they read it. A larger one is limit.input-too-large and nothing is written. predict, eval, describe: the largest model file read. A larger one is limit.input-too-large. predict from standard input (the operand - or none): the CSV is held in memory, so this is also the most bytes of standard input read. More is limit.input-too-large\"}},\"required\":[\"model-file\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"outputSchema\":{\"$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"One JSON object on one line. ok is false exactly when errors is present; error is its first element. A dry run (fit --dry-run) has ok true, exit 9, dry_run and planned_actions. No float appears: every decimal is a string with its digits exact.\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ok\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"command\":{\"const\":\"ml\"},\"schema\":{\"const\":\"ml.v1\"},\"data\":{\"$ref\":\"#/$defs/data\"},\"dry_run\":{\"const\":true},\"planned_actions\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"oneOf\":[{\"type\":\