les\",\"limits\",\"authority\"]},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true,\"openWorldHint\":false}},{\"name\":\"runs_list\",\"title\":\"runs list\",\"description\":\"Fit, apply and score a model on a CSV file, with the refusals of a tool an agent can read. Usage of the command line this tool is: `ml runs list ...`. Values the library refuses (ranges, conflicts between flags, unknown columns) come back as a tool error with the rule, the exit code and the repair.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"limit\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0,\"maximum\":1000000,\"default\":1000,\"description\":\"predict: the most rows in one page of predictions, at least 1. describe: the most category strings listed for each categorical column and the most rows of the importance table, at least 1 (a longer table lists the best ranks). runs list: the most run records listed, at least 1\"},\"max-bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0,\"maximum\":268435456,\"default\":16777216,\"description\":\"fit: the largest model file written, the limit predict and eval apply when they read it. A larger one is limit.input-too-large and nothing is written. predict, eval, describe: the largest model file read. A larger one is limit.input-too-large. predict from standard input (the operand - or none): the CSV is held in memory, so this is also the most bytes of standard input read. More is limit.input-too-large\"},\"dir\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"the directory of run records, relative to the server's root\"}},\"required\":[\"dir\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"outputSchema\":{\"$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"One JSON object on one line. ok is false exactly when errors is present; error is its first element. A dry run (fit --dry-run) has ok true, exit 9, dry_run and planned_actions. No float appears: every decimal is a string with its digits exact.\",\